  "term": "amusia",
  "definition": "Amusia is a loss or marked defect in the ability to understand, appreciate, remember, or produce music. It is described as the musical counterpart of aphasia, with forms affecting musical performance, musical comprehension, distorted musical perception, or musical memory.",
